{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T14:09:51.665Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e74d96e3f26b4206b5d49524","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T14:09:51.665Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-18T14:09:51.665Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Ranked by expected agent value per token, qualitatively. 1. A pre-create SDK guard avoids a subprocess and feeding candidate titles and distributions back to an agent on each create. Existing pre-create CLI and ranking primitives do not supply a typed stop/continue/review result. 2. Work selection could connect orientation and claim, but the host already orders work and eligibility depends on current claims and dependencies. 3. Escalation could price a missed handoff, but triage already emits needs_human and a gate accepts custom questions. Backlog triage already streams. The 63-item public baseline has 12 open items and no open item delivering the guard."}]}],"before_hash":"e8ebd900c10abbead5bf5f03f431347c5f24c5dbed198e9a0651b68ef4f13c89","after_hash":"e1c560753b77e5cbca1429e16f26df8a8abbe1652b58a47aca473d1a52a441c0","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"417c66eb2ca9a5556753af6b724095e4e8d55f38f09a158f4256c97c103ae0e0"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T14:11:53.340Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-astra","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e74d96e3f26b4206b5d49524","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-astra","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T14:11:53.338Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Design: expose a read-only SDK call and jev guard-create. Use the certified full tracker read and existing title retriever, typed choice request, model admission and optional digest-bound calibration. Retain one overflow candidate so a negative decision on a truncated list abstains. Apply a conservative probability floor, honor stricter settings and disabled fitted policies, and return compact counters and token usage. Fail closed on invalid input or incomplete tracker reads. An unavailable decision endpoint yields a typed abstention."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T14:11:53.340Z"}],"before_hash":"e1c560753b77e5cbca1429e16f26df8a8abbe1652b58a47aca473d1a52a441c0","after_hash":"ebc56aebe81a7fc628607695a0d3c969e942494849548809e36c0f0727bfdbd3","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"574376b59f14f418da1114965988ead2d5d58cb3c17eb11db1b764e94f346024"}
